"""
Hosted command-line argument access for Actus applications.

This module is available only when the selected target has a hosted process
environment. It exposes a bounded cursor instead of changing `main()` or
exposing native pointers. The first value produced by `next_arg` is the host
executable path (`argv[0]`); user-supplied values follow in their original
order. Use `count` to inspect the total before reading values.

Typical use:

    erg created = arguments();
    case dat created {
        Result.Ok(state) => {
            erg total = count(arguments: abs state);
            erg storage = Buffer[4096];
            erg next = next_arg(arguments: ins state, buffer: ins storage);
        },
        Result.Err(error) => { },
    };

Every read writes from buffer offset zero. The caller owns the `Buffer` and
must provide enough capacity; the API never grows or retains that buffer.
"""
open error;

"""Re-export the bounded process argument cursor and reader operations."""
open arguments;
